--- !u!114 &4191475704530158341
MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 0
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 7559861644087182071}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: ac6a2fb93f85841b0bc4fbb0fdea6c24, type: 3}
  m_Name: 
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Assembly-CSharp::LoreRevealManager
  yourselfEntries:
  - lines:
    - speaker: 1
      text: Yeah, so I hear you lost your memories.
    - speaker: 1
      text: Must be nice not to be cursed with all the knowledge in the world at
        once.
    - speaker: 1
      text: "I\u2019ll throw you a bone, and give you some intel."
    - speaker: 1
      text: "I\u2019ll throw you a bone, and give you some intel."
    - speaker: 1
      text: "You\u2019re a watchmaker\u2019s apprentice, a horologist who tends to
        clocks and gizmos\u2026 but somehow you ended up here. "
    - speaker: 1
      text: "Who knows, maybe you were sacrificed to Yog-Sothoth or something. Well,
        I know but I\u2019m not paid enough to be an educator."
  - lines:
    - speaker: 1
      text: "You want more info dumps about yourself? How self-centered. Your name
        was something stupid, like Willbur? No, Wilhelmina? It started with a \u201CW\u201D
        I think\u2026."
    - speaker: 1
      text: "If it was my place to say, you\u2019d look like a Will of some variety.
        Maybe I\u2019ll just call you \u2018Big Dubba Ewe."
  - lines:
    - speaker: 1
      text: "Brooo, you\u2019re so boring, what, want me to trauma dump on you? With
        your own trauma? That\u2019s freaked up. "
    - speaker: 1
      text: "You\u2019re like, an orphan or something, idk, maybe your boss didn\u2019t
        sacrifice you, fine, but maybe you wish he had."
  - lines:
    - speaker: 1
      text: Another one, Huh? Your favorite color is green. I think it looks like
        vomit, but whatever.
  - lines:
    - speaker: 1
      text: "Another one, Huh? If you ever do get back home, there\u2019s a white
        cat that\u2019s taken up residence in your apartment."
  - lines:
    - speaker: 1
      text: "Another one, Huh? You accidentally ended up in the red light district
        once, because you read \u201CWhoreology\u201D as \u201CHorology\u201D."
    - speaker: 1
      text: "Yikes, that\u2019s an awkward social interaction, are you dyslexic?
        It doesn\u2019t say on your file\u2026."
  - lines:
    - speaker: 1
      text: "Another one, Huh? One time you stayed up for three days without sleeping
        because you wanted to catch Santa in the act of delivering your gifts, but
        he never came\u2026. yeowch."
  - lines:
    - speaker: 1
      text: "Another one, Huh? \u2026 wait, you\u2019re so boring there\u2019s nothing
        else to say. Bummer, dude."
  worldEntries:
  - lines:
    - speaker: 1
      text: "Yeah so you\u2019re probably wondering how we got here\u2026."
    - speaker: 1
      text: "It\u2019s whatever, it\u2019s more important what here even is, right?"
  - lines:
    - speaker: 1
      text: 'The pocket watch dimension, as it has been so aptly named, is a pocket
        dimension at the junction between space and time that Yog-Sothoth has full
        jurisdiction over. '
    - speaker: 1
      text: "It would be pretty metal actually if we weren\u2019t in agony all the
        time as our flesh was constantly dying away and re-generating itself since
        time doesn\u2019t actually exist."
    - speaker: 1
      text: Man, is that why humans are always so tired?
  - lines:
    - speaker: 1
      text: "You wanna know about the guy who\u2019s torturing you? No, actually
        it\u2019s not Satan believe it or not, he has his own jurisdiction. "
    - speaker: 1
      text: Yog-Sothoth primarily deals with criminals who have committed offenses
        that ruptured the space time continuum.
    - speaker: 1
      text: " So\u2026 you\u2019re the first guest we\u2019ve had in a while."
  - lines:
    - speaker: 1
      text: "What do I look like? A database? Fine, how about I tell you what happened
        to the last person who ended up here \u2013 well the last few maybe\u2026"
    - speaker: 1
      text: "There were those Babylonians and Sumerians who established the sexagesimal
        (base-60) system for your modern minutes and seconds, Aristotle and Saint
        Augustine, since they couldn\u2019t shut their mouths about "
    - speaker: 1
      text: "\u2018the nature of time\u2019 and all that, OH, and Christiaan Huygens,
        the pendulum clock guy! Hey\u2026 how did YOU end up here of all people?"
  - lines:
    - speaker: 1
      text: "I can tell you\u2019re homesick, or maybe that\u2019s just your natural
        complexion. Don\u2019t worry though, I\u2019ll hook you up with the deets
        on your home world. "
    - speaker: 1
      text: "Lemme just check my sources, I think the world you came from was nuked?
        No, wait, it went into the next ice age? No, no, no, that was a different
        one\u2026 "
    - speaker: 1
      text: "You came from Jupiter, since you\u2019re stupider, right? That one has
        a great big red spot!"
  - lines:
    - speaker: 1
      text: "Hey, buddy, the horrors getting you down? Yog-Sothoth isn\u2019t THAT
        bad of a guy, like sure, he\u2019s like the biggest gatekeeper around but
        he is pretty girlboss if you ask me. "
    - speaker: 1
      text: "I mean, when you\u2019re like the boss of the past, present, AND future,
        I\u2019m sure it\u2019s a lot of work. What about gaslighting? Uh\u2026 let
        me get back to you on that one."
  - lines:
    - speaker: 1
      text: "You look like you\u2019d be passively interested in the dark arts\u2026
        I\u2019ll tell you something cool as nails."
    - speaker: 1
      text: "There\u2019s a ritual involving Yog-Sothoth that makes use of the \u201Cessential
        salts\u201D of a deceased individual to resurrect them from the dead!"
    - speaker: 1
      text: "How\u2019s that for spell components? You don\u2019t have someone you
        wanted to bring back\u2026 do you?"
  - lines:
    - speaker: 1
      text: "The Shopkeep? Why do you want to know anything about that weirdo. He
        just loiters in his little stall all day, selling snake oil and cancer or
        whatever\u2026."
    - speaker: 1
      text: "Only an iiiiidiot would buy anything from him. Right\u2026?"
  - lines:
    - speaker: 1
      text: 'You wanna know about my boy Dial? Turtle of many shells? Kelp walker
        of many names? The Sun Dial before time? '
    - speaker: 1
      text: "Idk, he\u2019s just a chill guy. He likes to point out the potential
        in people and then harass it out of them. 10/10 honestly."
  - lines:
    - speaker: 1
      text: "Fine, this is my last secret. We, the rat king, ARE a polycule. Now,
        don\u2019t ever let me see your face around these parts again!"
  - lines:
    - speaker: 1
      text: "Fuggetabout it. Quit asking me questions\u2026 pick a different topic
        at the very least! I\u2019m burnt out on world building. Laaaaameeeeee."
  metaEntries:
  - lines:
    - speaker: 1
      text: 'Did you know-- this would have been a puzzle game if any of the devs
        knew how to write puzzles? '
  - lines:
    - speaker: 1
      text: Did you know-- the project manager dev Colton has a cat named Moe who
        loves to eat plastic?
  - lines:
    - speaker: 1
      text: Did you know-- the character artist and narrative designer Leslie talked
        about DnD and soft skills to a captive audience of over 100 people?
  - lines:
    - speaker: 1
      text: 'Did you know-- the game''s animator Krepta has two widdle bitty babbies
        named Milkshake and Brownie who are her greatest inspirations, her muses,
        her very helpful helpers (they laid on her computer while she was drawing). '
  - lines:
    - speaker: 1
      text: 'Did you know-- this game was originally going to be about therapy in
        an elevator? '
  - lines:
    - speaker: 1
      text: That's all, the devs are out of interesting things to say-- we hope you
